From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 19:48:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03335/11362] [outer-loop] arc: goal-bias v1 (fixed
 order-prior) REFUTED -- 1/11 no lift, crashed the working game

Built GoalBiasValueHead (zero-shot distance-to-win prior over the arc_agi3_goal_induction hypothesis
classes: object-count+color-count+1-coverage) wired as explorer_goalbias (best-first A* frontier).
Same harness/games/budget as the 1/11 undirected baseline: goal-bias reaches first-win on 1/11 (NO
lift) AND crashed the one working game (lp85 20->437 actions, eff 2.0069->0.0042) by detouring
best-first toward 'more ordered' states -- lp85's win is not a consolidation. Refuted as a design: a
FIXED directional bias cannot work (games reward different directions: clear/build/toggle); the
no-lift result is weight-robust. The lever requires ONLINE direction-induction: stay direction-
agnostic until the env levels_completed signal reveals the rewarded hypothesis, then commit. The
fixed prior is preserved as the refuted seed; online-confirmation explorer is the next iteration.
Gate decision unchanged: NOT gate-ready. (Default explorer behavior unchanged -- opt-in policy variant.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
